course: dictionary
lesson: 4899
title: Illegally: breaking the law
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Adverbs tell you more about a verb: how, when or where something happens. Illegally tells you how something was done. Look at the word's parts: legal means allowed by the law, and il- here means not, so illegally means in a way that is against the law.
explain: «Some lenders charge huge interest, so £200 borrowed can grow to £400 owed; a loan shark is someone who lends illegally at huge cost.» The word lends tells you the action, and illegally tells you the lending breaks the law. Check it by swapping in your meaning: "a loan shark is someone who lends in a way that is against the law at huge cost." It still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: «Many lorises are caught illegally for the pet trade; all lorises are protected by international law.» The clue is protected by law. Catching lorises illegally means breaking that protection. Notice that illegally always sits next to the action it describes, such as caught or parked.
fact: Illegally is an adverb: it describes how an action is done, as in «parked illegally».
fact: «Illegally downloaded» means downloaded in a way that breaks the law.
fact: «Illegally dumped» means left in a place where the law says it must not be left.
fact: Tax evasion means illegally not paying tax, which can lead to fines or prison.
fact: «Bombing» in graffiti slang means spraying lots of tags quickly, usually illegally; it has nothing to do with real bombs.
exercise: «They parked illegally outside the school.» What does illegally mean here? | Next to the school gate | Very quickly | In a neat, tidy way | *In a way that is against the law
exercise: Ella says, «Those otters were caught illegally from the wild.» What does the word tell us? | *The otters were taken in a way that broke the law | The otters were found in a park | The otters were happy to be caught | The otters were very hungry
exercise: «The man dumped the rubbish illegally.» Which word tells how the rubbish was dumped? | man | rubbish | *illegally | the
test: Tax evasion means illegally not paying tax. What does illegally mean in this phrase? | Late, after the due date | Very loudly | *Against the law | Happily
test: Graffiti slang "bombing" means spraying lots of tags quickly, usually illegally. What does illegally mean in this sentence? | Very slowly | Using real bombs | *In a way that breaks the law | In a tidy, neat way
exam: Which phrase best shows that someone broke a law? | happily singing | very tall | *illegally dumped | slept soundly
